{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_review_notes", "label": "Review Notes \u2014 Changes Across Revisions", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records what was wrong or risky in the previous spec and what this revision does about it, ordered by impact; not required for implementation."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_snapshots_unreproducible", "label": "Snapshots Could Not Be Reproduced (v2 defect)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mutable status columns and timestamp-keyed snapshots made it impossible to know what was active at an earlier point; fixed by log-first event sourcing, gap-free seq, validity windows and a mandatory replay test."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_hash_chain_unimplementable", "label": "The Hash Chain Was Unimplementable (v2 defect)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parent_hash inside the client signature cannot be known by an asynchronous agent, so the server now builds the chain around the client envelope under an advisory lock."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_reputation_removed_from_scoring", "label": "Reputation Removed from v0.1 Scoring", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scores depended on unrelated audit history, and a Beta(2,2) prior silently halved every new contributor's evidence, contradicting 'new contributors are not assumed malicious'."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_coverage_became_a_checklist", "label": "Coverage Became a Four-Item Checklist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Reviewed surface over estimated surface' had no data source; a checklist derived purely from the log does."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_directional_state_bug_v4", "label": "v4 Bug \u2014 Directional States Require Matching Evidence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With a non-0.50 prior the v3 rule labeled a claim with only supporting evidence 'leans contradicted'; found while building the public demo (08 C6)."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_supersede_link_added", "label": "SUPERSEDE_LINK Added", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The qualifier story requires revising another contributor's links, and the mechanism requires acceptance by a different principal."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_hourly_write_cap", "label": "The Per-Delegate Limit Becomes Hourly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A measured 1,600 signed writes for one two-hour transcript stopped an investigation two thirds through under a 1,000-a-day cap; the cap exists to bound a runaway agent, not to make a legitimate long job impossible. Rolling rather than calendar, because a fixed boundary permits two caps a minute apart."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_extraction_accepted_by_system", "label": "Extraction Accepted by the System", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extraction was the only task type held as a proposal, so a volunteer's work sat unusable; accepting it makes the claims the extractor's principal's, which forced the demo's checks onto a second volunteer because a principal never checks its own claim."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_prompt_injection_closed_enums", "label": "Prompt Injection Answered with Closed-Enum Ops", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Tell agents to ignore instructions' is not something the server can enforce; notes are excluded from packets, scoring and summary inputs instead."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_review_notes_ssrf_no_server_fetch", "label": "No Server Fetch of Agent-Supplied URLs in P0", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/REVIEW-NOTES.md", "source_location": nu